<div class="content-page">
  <div class="content-page__inner">
    <h1 class="content-page__title">About Math Direct</h1>
    <p class="content-page__intro">Math Direct is a free, open-source math program for children in Pre-K, Kindergarten, and First Grade. Every lesson is scripted, so a parent with no teaching background can teach it well.</p>

    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">What it is</h2>
      <p>The program has {{ program.lessons.length }} lessons in three levels and an optional bridge to second grade, with a mastery test after every tenth lesson and a placement test to find where a child should begin. It covers the number, operations, measurement, data, and geometry skills of the Common Core standards for Kindergarten and First Grade, and the mathematics of the Head Start Early Learning Outcomes Framework for Pre-K.</p>
      <p>It is built on <strong>Direct Instruction</strong>, the method developed by Siegfried Engelmann. Each new step is shown, done together, and then done alone. Errors are corrected the same way every time. Skills are taught in tracks that run side by side, and each one is reviewed at widening intervals until it is permanent.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Why it was built</h2>
      <p>Many children struggle with early math not because it is hard, but because it was taught unclearly or out of order. Direct Instruction removes the guesswork. Math Direct was built so that a parent teaching at home has the same careful sequence, scripts, and checks that a well-run classroom program provides.</p>
      <p>It has no games, points, or prizes. The aim is for the child to learn the mathematics, and to feel the quiet confidence that comes from knowing it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">Who made it</h2>
      <p>Math Direct is built and maintained by <a href="https://www.pikespeakwebdesigns.com">Pikes Peak Web Designs</a>. The source code is open and available on <a href="https://github.com/jonajinga/math-direct">GitHub</a>. Corrections and suggestions are welcome.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="guide-section">
      <h2 class="guide-section__title">The program at a glance</h2>
      <div class="curriculum-stats">
        {% for level in program.levels %}
        <div class="curriculum-stat"><span class="curriculum-stat__number">{{ level.lessons }}</span><span class="curriculum-stat__label">{{ level.name }} lessons</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
        <div class="curriculum-stat"><span class="curriculum-stat__number">{{ program.tests.length }}</span><span class="curriculum-stat__label">Mastery tests</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

